# Crime Novelist: "Whenever you sacrifice an artifact, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature and add {R}." A Treasure sacrificed to pay
# for a spell is the cost of a mana ability, so the trigger is a triggered mana ability (CR 605.1b, 605.4a): it resolves as the Treasure's
# mana is made, never using the stack, and the red it adds is there to pay Lightning Bolt's {R} with the Treasure's own mana left over.
# Turn 1: five Mox Rubies pay for Crime Novelist and Reckless Ransacking, which makes the Treasure. Turn 3: Bolt is paid with the
# Treasure, whose mana is {R} (chosen), and the Novelist's {R} stays in the pool.

[Bot1 Deck]
Crime Novelist
Reckless Ransacking
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

